{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/377855-looking-for-fresh-blood-for-long-running-skype-pbp-2-5-exalted","id":377855,"title":"Looking for fresh blood for long-running Skype/PBP 2.5 Exalted!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-21T23:48:01-08:00","id":377855,"title":"Looking for fresh blood for long-running Skype/PBP 2.5 Exalted!","content":"Hail! A few friends and I are looking for some new faces for an old game! We've been at it for two and a half years now, and we're about to come up on a rather chaotic moment which is prime for some introductions. If you're interested, do let me know.<br /> <br /> Right, details...<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> Exalted 2.5 (some houserules, such as unified XP costs and new backgrounds)<br /> <b>Medium:</b> Skype, once per week Thursdays 9:30pm-1:30am EST Friday; Roleplay Online (play by post during the week); and Roll20 (when we need a map for combat). Existing players have regrettably opposed schedules and commitments that make day/time changes almost impossible (apart from moving times back or forward by perhaps half an hour). Punctuality/reliability is critical-- we're here for years of madness and seek similar souls.<br /> <b>Setting:</b> Canon Exalted (with many additions, naturally; we have a document). Currently about twenty years after the start of Core (so well into the Time of Tumult). We're off the beaten paths in the East.<br /> <b>Balance:</b> Seesaws wildly between combat and investigation/social encounters. Lately it's been more about social interaction (and, to be fair, engineering). Most combat is low-intensity (one player does not have a combat excellency), but every so often someone decides to &quot;try out&quot; the full system and things get hairy. Generally the storyline adapts to the players' interests (though not always the characters').<br /> <b>New Characters:</b> Most concepts for Solars, Abyssals, Infernals, Lunars, and Sidereals are welcome; other Exalt types are not. There will be some extra starting XP or other effort to create parity with the other PCs. Do plan a heroic motivation, though-- the ST's exact words were, &quot;Be big d**n heroes!&quot;<br /> <b>Existing Characters:</b> One Twilight Solar working to become the greatest healer in all Creation, one extremely loyalist Infernal Fiend with very strange history, and one bedraggled Sidereal who knows who everyone is.<br /> <br /> And there you have it. More details (than anyone could probably want) are in the RPoL threads: <a href=\"http://rpol.net/game.cgi?gi=53735\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpol.net/game.cgi?gi=53735</a><br /> If you have any questions feel free to ask here, or we can get in touch with the ST over Skype. Happy gaming!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3914,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3914-cassus","user":"Cassus","date":". 01-22-2015, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3914-cassus","name":"Cassus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T07:35:22-08:00","id":378042,"title":"","content":"Interest. Dunno what I'd propose to play, yet. Definitely something Solaroid (thats all I own books for). The only character I've tried to make and have yet to get off the ground in a meaninful fashion is a Solar martial artist that advances in Solar Hero and Infernal Monster with a cut-down version of the akuma charm that lets both forms be active at once.<br /> <br /> On a side note, I tried to access the RPOL stuff. Cant get in. Can you post the house-rules here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":771,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/771-starmage21","user":"Starmage21","date":".  Looked at RPOL page 01-22-2015, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/771-starmage21","name":"Starmage21","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T19:12:31-08:00","id":378601,"title":"","content":"A Solaroid? Well, it'd certainly fit with the level of the rest of the party. We do have some martial artists, but what sort of motivation do you have in mind? Can't speak to custom content myself, of course, but the ST does encourage creativity.<br /> <br /> <br /> As far as posting houserules... Right, I'd forgotten the changes to the way content ratings worked. Sure, here goes!<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">1: Health Levels.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Base health levels are x3, Ox Body and similar are x5, extras get 1 of each level of health from -0 counting down to -4 and then incapacitated. You begin to 'bleed' as you lose levels, taking more levels of damage increasingly rapidly as your body loses integrity: but can roll to stabilize and clot.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">2: War Rules:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The ST is currently working on 'fixing' the rules for Mass Combat. Has been some time, in fact.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A: So far the only change is that Magnitude is calculated based on the following rubric. This applies to determining Magnitude for combat bonuses; charms that target a particular magnitude use the old system.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 1 Person = 0</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 2 People = 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 5 People = 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 10 People = 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 20 People = 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 50 People = 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">100 People = 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">200 People = 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Etc.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A1: A person may not count as both a special character in a unit and the source of the unit's base profile: they can either be a trooper or a hero, not both.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Many more changes are to follow as the ST gets a better sense of where the flaws are in the system and thinks of ways to correct them, one of which (Still pending review and play testing, so not yet implemented) is to more strictly enforce the &quot;original stunt&quot; rule for non-mass charms in mass combat.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3: Experience.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This game while largely conducted over RPoL, is also partially conducted over Skype and Roll 20. When we have had a Roll20/Skype session the players gain XP as per normal for Exalted.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">However part of the reason that these games were combine into one over this medium is that they were happening too infrequently over Skype, so...</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A: When the game goes more than a week without a session in our other format everyone who has been participating adequately by the ST's estimation will gain 1 to 4 XP based on their level of participation and activity, the more active the more XP.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Characters must sill reach periods of Down Time to spend XP, or use workarounds such as favored abilities and Training charms.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">B: When the players complete a Story or other significant event, instead of the normal XP awards the storyteller will award dots in backgrounds reflecting their increasing reputations and resources. These can include artifacts, connections, Fame, and so forth. These awards will be lesser or greater depending on the characters involvement and active attempts to develop backgrounds but will in general total no more than 3 dots of backgrounds at one time, all else must be paid for with XP.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3914-cassus","name":"Cassus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}